  "rationale": "The fixed 1, 4, and 12-condition stationary-bootstrap sensitivity envelope protects against several dependence horizons but cannot adapt to the observed chronological dependence of each loss or PnL series. The corrected Politis-White selector estimates an expected stationary-bootstrap block length from the series autocovariance structure. The implementation rounds the estimate upward, caps it at one quarter of the population, and adds it to rather than replaces the frozen fixed lengths. The final interval remains the widest lower and upper bound across every included block length, so this amendment can only preserve or tighten promotion. Log-loss, Brier-score, and economic PnL series select their horizons independently. No target, threshold, candidate family, economic rule, prompt, or authority was used or relaxed.",
